{title: 358 - Far and Near the Fields Are Teeming}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Church}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]Far and near the [Edim]fields [F]are teeming [Bb]with [C7/Bb]the [Bb]sheaves of [F]ripened grain;
[F/C]Far and near their gold [G7]is [Edim]gleaming [F]O'er the sunny [Edim]slope [F]and plain.
[Bb]Lord of [C7/Bb]harvest, [Bb/F]send [F]forth reapers! Hear us [Bb/F]Lord, to [F]Thee [Edim]we [F]cry;
[Am]Send them now the [F]sheaves [Gm]to gather, [C7]Ere the harvesttime pass [Am]by.

Refrain:
[Am]Lord of [Bb]harvest, [Am]send forth reapers!
[F]Hear us Lord,to [Edim]Thee [F]we cry;
[Bb]Send them [Gm/Bb]now [Bb]the sheaves [F]to gather,
[F/A]Ere the [Bb/F]harvest-time [Edim]pass [F]by.

Verse 2:
[F]Send them [Edim]forth [F]with [Bb]morn's first beaming,
[F/C]Send them in [Edim]the [F]noon-tides's glare;
[Bb]When [C7/Bb]the [Bb/F]sun's [F]last rays are streaming,
[Am]bid them [F]gather [C7]everywhere.

Verse 3:
[F]O thou, [Edim]whom [F]thy [Bb]Lord is sending,
[F/C]gather now [Edim]the [F]sheaves [Edim]of [F]gold;
[Bb]Heavenward then [F]at evening wending
[Am]Thou shalt [F]come [Gm]with [C7]joy [F/C]untold.
